# WiLL 3D Pole Configurator — production frontend env
#
# Copy this file to `.env.production` (or set the var in your host's build env)
# before running `npm run build` for a production deploy.
#
# Vite inlines any variable prefixed `VITE_` at BUILD TIME. The value baked into
# the bundle is whatever was set when `npm run build` ran — there is no runtime
# lookup. Rebuild after changing it.

# Base URL of the deployed geometry-service (FastAPI CAD/BIM backend).
# No trailing slash. The frontend appends /jobs, /jobs/{id}, /files/{name},
# /generate, and /health to this base.
#
# PLACEHOLDER — a human fills in the real App Runner URL AFTER the service is
# created (docs/DEPLOY.md, "AWS — App Runner from ECR"). Example shape (NOT a
# real app): https://abc123xyz.us-east-1.awsapprunner.com
# (fly.io was the earlier prep and was not taken — Tyler 8/19.)
VITE_GEOMETRY_URL=https://REPLACE-ME.us-east-1.awsapprunner.com

# --- Dev note ---
# In development the var is normally left UNSET: src/lib/geometry.ts falls back to
# http://localhost:8000, matching `./geometry-service/run.sh`. Only set
# VITE_GEOMETRY_URL locally if your geometry-service listens elsewhere.
